        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__stats">
        <div class="hero__stat">
          <span class="hero__stat-value">300</span>
          <span class="hero__stat-label">Pieces Minimum</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__stat">
          <span class="hero__stat-value">4-Way</span>
          <span class="hero__stat-label">Stretch Fabric</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__stat">
          <span class="hero__stat-value">{companyAge}</span>
          <span class="hero__stat-label">Years Experience</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__stat">
          <span class="hero__stat-value">30-40</span>
          <span class="hero__stat-label">Days Production</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="trust">
    <div class="trust__container">
      <div class="trust__items">
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">🛡️</span>
          <span>OEKO-TEX Standard 100</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">♻️</span>
          <span>GRS Recycled</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">🤝</span>
          <span>BSCI Social Compliance</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">⭐</span>
          <span>ISO 9001 Quality</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Introduction</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Yoga Pants Manufacturer for Growing Activewear Brands</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>As a specialized yoga pants manufacturer based in Bangladesh, SDF Clothing understands the unique requirements of activewear brands seeking reliable production partners. The yoga apparel market demands exceptional fabric performance, precise construction, and consistent quality across production runs. Our facility delivers on these requirements with minimum orders of 300 pieces, making professional manufacturing accessible to emerging brands and established labels expanding their product lines.</p>
        
        <p>Bangladesh has emerged as a global leader in activewear manufacturing due to specialized expertise in performance fabrics, competitive labor costs, and established infrastructure for garment production. Our yoga pants production leverages these advantages, offering international brands access to factory-direct pricing without compromising on quality standards. The 300-piece minimum allows you to test market response with manageable inventory while benefiting from bulk production economics.</p>
        
        <p>Our yoga pants manufacturing focuses on the technical aspects that matter most to practitioners: 4-way stretch for unrestricted movement, moisture-wicking properties for comfort during practice, compression for muscle support, and durable construction that withstands repeated washing and wearing. We work with nylon-spandex, polyester-spandex, cotton-spandex, and recycled fabric blends to match your performance requirements and sustainability goals.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Product Range</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">What We Manufacture</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Our yoga pants production encompasses multiple styles designed for different practice preferences and market segments. Each style maintains our commitment to performance fabrics and quality construction while offering distinct aesthetic and functional characteristics. We manufacture all styles from 300 pieces minimum, with the ability to mix styles within larger orders for brand collections.</p>
        
        <p>High-waist yoga pants represent our most popular style, providing coverage and core support during practice. The elevated waistband typically sits above the navel, featuring 3-4 inch elastic construction for secure fit without digging or rolling. High-waist designs are particularly favored for yoga and pilates where core engagement and coverage during inversions are priorities. Our high-waist yoga pants use reinforced stitching at the waistband-seam junction to prevent separation during extended wear.</p>
        
        <p>Flare yoga pants offer a fashion-forward alternative to fitted silhouettes, featuring fitted legs through the thigh with gradual widening from the knee downward. This style combines yoga pant performance with bohemian aesthetic appeal, popular in lifestyle yoga markets and studio-to-street transitions. Flare yoga pants require careful pattern grading to ensure the flare opens at the correct point while maintaining fit through the hips and thighs. We produce flare styles in 26-30 inch inseams for standard heights, with custom lengths available upon request.</p>
        
        <p>Capri-length yoga pants end mid-calf, typically at 19-21 inch inseams, providing cooler options for warmer climates or practitioners who prefer shorter lengths. Capris maintain all performance features of full-length styles including 4-way stretch, moisture-wicking, and waistband construction. The cropped length requires careful hem finishing to prevent rolling or curling during movement. We offer capri styles in both fitted and flare silhouettes to match your brand aesthetic.</p>
        
        <p>Full-length yoga pants in 28-32 inch inseams represent the traditional yoga pant silhouette, suitable for most heights and practice types. Full-length styles provide full leg coverage and can be worn for yoga, pilates, barre, and general fitness activities. Our full-length production includes ankle-zip options for easy on/off over footwear, and bootcut variations for practitioners who prefer slight flare at the hem. All full-length styles feature gusseted crotch construction for comfort and durability during deep stretches and wide-legged poses.</p>
        
        <p>Yoga pants with pocket options address the growing demand for functionality in activewear. We offer side seam pockets for minimalist storage, waistband pockets for securing small items during practice, and back zip pockets for valuables. Pocket integration requires careful construction to maintain fabric stretch and prevent bulk or distortion. Our pocket placements are tested during movement to ensure items remain secure without interfering with practice.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Style</th>
              <th>Typical Inseam</th>
              <th>Key Features</th>
              <th>Best For</th>
              <th>Price Tier</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>High-Waist Yoga Pants</td>
              <td>28-32"</td>
              <td>Above-navel waistband, core support, coverage</td>
              <td>Yoga, pilates, inversions</td>
              <td>$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Flare Yoga Pants</td>
              <td>28-30"</td>
              <td>Fitted thigh, gradual flare, fashion styling</td>
              <td>Lifestyle yoga, studio-to-street</td>
              <td>$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Capri Yoga Pants</td>
              <td>19-21"</td>
              <td>Cropped length, cooler wear, full performance</td>
              <td>Warmer climates, shorter preferences</td>
              <td>$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Full-Length Yoga Pants</td>
              <td>28-32"</td>
              <td>Traditional silhouette, ankle-zip options</td>
              <td>General fitness, all practice types</td>
              <td>$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Yoga Pants with Pockets</td>
              <td>28-32"</td>
              <td>Side/waist/back pockets, functional storage</td>
              <td>Active lifestyle, functionality focus</td>
              <td>$$</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
          <caption>All styles available from 300 pieces minimum. Custom inseam lengths available with tech pack.</caption>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Production Process</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Our Manufacturing Process</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Our yoga pants manufacturing follows a structured process from design brief to final shipment, ensuring quality control at each stage. The process typically spans 60-75 days for first-time orders including sampling and production, with 45-60 days for repeat orders using approved fabrics and patterns. Understanding this timeline helps you plan product launches and inventory management effectively.</p>
        
        <p>The process begins with design brief review, where we analyze your specifications including fabric requirements, size charts, technical drawings, and target pricing. Our team provides feedback on feasibility, suggests alternatives for cost optimization, and clarifies any technical questions. This stage typically takes 2-3 days and ensures alignment before sample development begins. We may request reference samples or detailed measurements if specifications are unclear.</p>
        
        <p>Fabric sourcing and development comes next, taking 10-15 days for standard fabrics and 15-20 days for custom fabric development. We source from our network of certified fabric suppliers in Bangladesh, providing swatches for your approval. If you require custom fabric development for specific colors, prints, or performance properties, we coordinate with mills to produce sample yardage. All fabrics are tested for GSM, stretch recovery, color fastness, and pilling resistance before bulk production.</p>
        
        <p>Sample development takes 15-20 days, during which we produce prototypes for your review. Initial samples focus on fit and construction, with subsequent samples refining details based on your feedback. We provide detailed measurement reports comparing samples to your specifications, along with wash testing results to verify fabric performance. You may request multiple sample rounds to perfect the design, though each round adds 7-10 days to the timeline. Sampling costs are separate from production costs but credited against bulk orders.</p>
        
        <p>Pattern grading follows sample approval, creating size sets from XS to 4XL based on your size chart or our standard size chart. Grading ensures proportional sizing across the range, maintaining fit consistency from smallest to largest sizes. This stage takes 3-5 days and includes measurement verification at each size point. We provide graded spec sheets for your records, documenting measurements for each size to facilitate future reorders.</p>
        
        <p>Bulk production spans 30-40 days from fabric receipt, beginning with cutting, sewing, and finishing operations. Cutting is performed by experienced operators using automated cutting machines for precision and material efficiency. Sewing lines are staffed by trained operators specializing in activewear construction, with quality checkpoints at each sewing operation. Finishing includes trimming, pressing, and final inspection before packaging. Throughout production, we conduct in-line quality checks and random inspections to catch issues early.</p>
        
        <p>Final quality inspection uses AQL 2.5 standards for major defects and AQL 4.0 for minor defects, ensuring statistically valid sampling for order acceptance. Inspection covers measurements, construction, stitching quality, fabric defects, and packaging compliance. We provide detailed inspection reports with photos for your review before shipment. Any defects found during inspection are rectified before goods leave our facility, though minor defects within AQL limits are accepted per industry standards.</p>
        
        <p>Packaging and shipping complete the process, taking 3-5 days for final preparation and documentation. We offer various packaging options from basic poly bags to custom retail packaging with branded hang tags. Shipping documentation includes commercial invoices, packing lists, certificates of origin, and any required export documentation. We coordinate with freight forwarders for air or ocean shipment based on your timeline and budget requirements.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Materials</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Fabric & Material Options</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Fabric selection is critical to yoga pants performance, affecting stretch, recovery, moisture management, and durability. We offer multiple fabric options optimized for different performance requirements and price points. All fabrics feature 4-way stretch for unrestricted movement and are tested for recovery to ensure the pants maintain shape through repeated wear and washing.</p>
        
        <p>Nylon-spandex blends, typically in 80/20 or 82/18 ratios, represent the premium choice for yoga pants. Nylon provides excellent durability, abrasion resistance, and a smooth hand feel, while spandex delivers the stretch and recovery essential for yoga practice. Nylon-spandex fabrics offer superior moisture-wicking compared to other blends, moving perspiration away from the skin for comfort during intense practice. These fabrics typically range from 200-280 GSM, with higher GSM providing more compression and opacity. Nylon-spandex is our recommendation for premium positioning and high-intensity practice.</p>
        
        <p>Polyester-spandex blends, usually 85/15 or 88/12, offer cost efficiency with good performance characteristics. Polyester provides excellent color retention, durability, and resistance to pilling, making it suitable for printed and solid-color yoga pants. While polyester-spandex has slightly less natural moisture-wicking than nylon, performance finishes can enhance moisture management. These fabrics typically range from 180-250 GSM and are ideal for value-positioned lines or fashion-focused yoga pants where performance requirements are moderate.</p>
        
        <p>Cotton-spandex blends, typically 92/8 or 95/5, provide natural fiber comfort with stretch capabilities. Cotton offers breathability and softness against the skin, appealing to practitioners seeking natural fiber options. The lower spandex content provides moderate stretch, suitable for gentle yoga and lifestyle wear rather than high-intensity practice. Cotton-spandex fabrics range from 180-220 GSM and are ideal for maternity yoga pants, casual yoga wear, and brands emphasizing natural materials.</p>
        
        <p>Recycled polyester-spandex fabrics, certified by GRS (Global Recycled Standard), provide sustainable options without compromising performance. These fabrics are made from post-consumer plastic bottles, processed into polyester fiber and blended with spandex for stretch. Recycled fabrics offer the same durability, color retention, and performance as virgin polyester, with the added benefit of environmental certification. GRS certification requires traceability throughout the supply chain, providing documentation for sustainability marketing. Recycled fabrics typically cost 10-15% more than conventional polyester but appeal to eco-conscious consumers.</p>
        
        <p>Bamboo-spandex blends, typically 95/5, offer natural antimicrobial properties and exceptional softness. Bamboo fabric is highly breathable and moisture-wicking, making it suitable for yoga practice. The fabric has a luxurious drape and natural sheen, differentiating it from synthetic options. Bamboo-spandex ranges from 160-200 GSM and is ideal for premium natural fiber positioning. However, bamboo fabrics require special care in washing to maintain longevity, which should be communicated to end consumers.</p>
        
        <p>Performance finishes can be applied to enhance fabric properties. Moisture-wicking finishes improve perspiration management on polyester and cotton blends. Anti-microbial treatments reduce odor buildup during extended wear. UV protection finishes add SPF ratings for outdoor practice. These finishes add cost but can differentiate your product in competitive markets. We recommend finishes based on your target market and positioning strategy.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Fabric</th>
              <th>Composition</th>
              <th>GSM Range</th>
              <th>Key Properties</th>
              <th>Best For</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Nylon-Spandex</td>
              <td>80/20 or 82/18</td>
              <td>200-280</td>
              <td>Premium stretch, moisture-wicking, durable</td>
              <td>Premium activewear, high-intensity</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Polyester-Spandex</td>
              <td>85/15 or 88/12</td>
              <td>180-250</td>
              <td>Color-fast, cost-efficient, pill-resistant</td>
              <td>Value positioning, fashion styles</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Cotton-Spandex</td>
              <td>92/8 or 95/5</td>
              <td>180-220</td>
              <td>Natural feel, breathable, soft</td>
              <td>Gentle yoga, natural fiber brands</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Recycled Polyester-Spandex</td>
              <td>85/15 (GRS certified)</td>
              <td>180-250</td>
              <td>Sustainable, durable, certified</td>
              <td>Eco-conscious brands, sustainability</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Bamboo-Spandex</td>
              <td>95/5</td>
              <td>160-200</td>
              <td>Antimicrobial, soft, luxurious</td>
              <td>Premium natural, luxury positioning</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
          <caption>All fabrics feature 4-way stretch. Custom GSM available with fabric development.</caption>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Bangladesh Advantage</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Why Source Yoga Pants from Bangladesh</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Bangladesh has established itself as a global hub for garment manufacturing, particularly in the activewear segment. The country's garment industry has evolved from basic cut-and-sew operations to sophisticated manufacturing capable of producing technical performance wear. This evolution, combined with competitive labor costs and established infrastructure, makes Bangladesh an ideal sourcing location for yoga pants production.</p>
        
        <p>Labor costs in Bangladesh are significantly lower than in China, Vietnam, or Turkey, translating to 15-25% cost savings on finished goods. However, low labor costs do not mean low quality. The Bangladeshi garment industry has invested heavily in worker training and skill development, particularly in specialized areas like activewear construction where precision and consistency are critical. Our operators receive regular training on the latest sewing techniques and quality standards for performance fabrics.</p>
        
        <p>Bangladesh's garment infrastructure includes specialized fabric mills capable of producing technical performance fabrics. While some specialized fabrics may still require import, the domestic supply of nylon-spandex, polyester-spandex, and cotton-spandex blends is well-established. This local sourcing reduces lead times and logistics costs compared to countries that rely entirely on imported fabrics. Our relationships with local fabric mills ensure priority allocation and consistent quality.</p>
        
        <p>The country's export-oriented garment industry has developed robust systems for international trade, including experienced freight forwarding, customs clearance, and documentation processes. Shipments from Bangladesh to major markets are routine and reliable, with multiple weekly sailings to Europe and North America. Air freight options are available for urgent orders, though ocean freight is more cost-effective for standard production volumes.</p>
        
        <p>Bangladesh garment factories have made significant investments in social compliance and workplace safety following the industry-wide improvements after 2013. Our facility holds BSCI certification, demonstrating adherence to international labor standards including fair wages, reasonable working hours, and safe working conditions. These certifications are increasingly important to consumers and retailers who prioritize ethical sourcing in their supply chains.</p>
        
        <p>Duty-free access to European markets through the Everything But Arms (EBA) arrangement provides Bangladesh garments with preferential tariff treatment, reducing import costs for EU customers. Similar preferential access exists for other markets including Canada, Australia, and Japan. This duty advantage can significantly impact landed costs, making Bangladesh-sourced yoga pants more competitive in these markets compared to garments from countries without preferential access.</p>
        
        <p>The Bangladesh garment industry has developed specialized expertise in knitwear production, which directly translates to yoga pants manufacturing. Knit fabric handling, stretch sewing techniques, and quality control for stretch garments are well-established skills in the country's workforce. This specialized expertise reduces the learning curve for new styles and ensures consistent quality across production runs.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">International Shipping</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Shipping to UK, USA, Australia & EU</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>We ship yoga pants to major international markets including the United Kingdom, United States, Australia, and European Union countries. Each market has specific requirements for documentation, duties, and shipping timelines that we navigate routinely. Our experience with international shipping ensures your goods arrive on time and with proper documentation for customs clearance.</p>
        
        <p>Shipments to the United Kingdom typically take 30-35 days by ocean freight, including transit time and customs clearance. Air freight options reduce this to 7-10 days at significantly higher cost. The UK applies import duties on garments from Bangladesh, though rates vary by fabric composition and declared value. We provide accurate Harmonized System (HS) codes and valuation to ensure proper duty calculation. Brexit has introduced additional documentation requirements, which we handle to ensure smooth customs clearance.</p>
        
        <p>United States shipments take 25-30 days by ocean freight to West Coast ports and 35-40 days to East Coast ports. Air freight takes 5-7 days to major US airports. The US maintains normal trade relations with Bangladesh, with standard MFN duty rates applying to most garments. Certain fabric compositions may qualify for preferential rates under trade agreements. We provide country of origin documentation and ensure compliance with US Customs and Border Protection requirements. US shipments also require fiber content labeling in English, which we include as standard practice.</p>
        
        <p>Australia shipments take 20-25 days by ocean freight to major ports including Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane. Air freight takes 7-10 days. Australia maintains a free trade agreement with Bangladesh that eliminates duties on many garments, though specific rules of origin must be met. We ensure our production processes meet these origin requirements to qualify for duty-free entry. Australia also has strict biosecurity requirements that we comply with through proper packaging and documentation.</p>
        
        <p>European Union shipments benefit from duty-free access under the Everything But Arms arrangement for least-developed countries. Ocean freight takes 28-32 days to Northern European ports and 32-38 days to Southern European ports. Air freight takes 5-8 days. EU countries require specific documentation including certificates of origin, commercial invoices with detailed descriptions, and conformity declarations for certain materials. We have extensive experience shipping to EU markets and ensure full compliance with all requirements.</p>
        
        <p>Documentation for all markets includes commercial invoices, packing lists, bills of lading, certificates of origin, and any required certificates for regulated materials. We provide all documentation in English and can arrange for translations if required by specific markets. Our documentation is prepared to meet both customs requirements and your internal accounting needs, with clear descriptions and accurate valuations.</p>
        
        <p>Incoterms can be structured according to your preferences, including FOB (Free On Board) Bangladesh for maximum control, CIF (Cost, Insurance, Freight) to destination port for convenience, or DDP (Delivered Duty Paid) for complete door-to-door service. We recommend FOB for experienced importers who have established freight forwarding relationships, as this typically provides the best overall cost. CIF and DDP options are available for brands seeking simplified logistics.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Certifications</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Quality Standards & Certifications</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Quality assurance and certification are fundamental to our yoga pants manufacturing process. We maintain multiple certifications that verify our commitment to quality, social responsibility, and environmental standards. These certifications provide assurance to your brand and end consumers that products are manufactured to international standards.</p>
        
        <p>OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certification applies to our fabrics, ensuring they are free from harmful substances including heavy metals, pesticides, and formaldehyde. This certification is particularly important for activewear that has prolonged skin contact during practice. OEKO-TEX testing covers all fabric components including base materials, dyes, and finishes. We provide OEKO-TEX certificates for each fabric lot, enabling you to substantiate claims about chemical safety in your marketing materials.</p>
        
        <p>GRS (Global Recycled Standard) certification applies to our recycled polyester fabrics, verifying the recycled content and ensuring traceability throughout the supply chain. GRS certification covers environmental and social criteria for recycled material production, including wastewater treatment, chemical restrictions, and labor practices. If you choose recycled fabrics for your yoga pants, GRS certification provides credible substantiation for sustainability claims and is increasingly required by major retailers for recycled content products.</p>
        
        <p>BSCI (Business Social Compliance Initiative) certification verifies our adherence to international labor standards including fair wages, reasonable working hours, prohibition of child labor, and safe working conditions. BSCI audits are conducted by independent third-party auditors and cover all aspects of social compliance. This certification is important for brands that prioritize ethical sourcing and need to demonstrate supply chain responsibility to stakeholders and consumers.</p>
        
        <p>ISO 9001 certification applies to our quality management system, ensuring consistent processes for production and quality control. ISO 9001 requires documented procedures for all critical processes, regular internal audits, and continuous improvement. This certification provides assurance that our quality systems are systematic and repeatable, reducing variability between production runs. For your brand, this means consistent fit, construction, and finish across orders.</p>
        
        <p>WRAP (Worldwide Responsible Accredited Production) certification is another social compliance certification we maintain, focusing specifically on workplace conditions and worker rights. WRAP certification covers similar ground to BSCI but with different audit methodology. Holding multiple social compliance certifications provides flexibility to meet various retailer requirements, as different buyers may specify different certification preferences in their vendor codes of conduct.</p>
        
        <p>Internal quality control processes supplement these certifications with day-to-day assurance. We conduct in-line inspections during production, measuring garments against specifications at critical checkpoints. Final inspection uses AQL (Acceptable Quality Limit) sampling standards to statistically determine if orders meet quality criteria. We maintain measurement records for each size and lot, enabling traceability if issues arise after delivery. These internal processes ensure certifications translate to actual quality in finished goods.</p>
      </div>
