        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">How to Get Started</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Starting your yoga pants production with SDF Clothing is a straightforward process designed to move from inquiry to delivery efficiently. The process begins with providing us with your requirements, after which we guide you through sampling, approval, and production. Understanding these steps upfront helps you prepare the information we need and set realistic timelines for your product launch.</p>
        
        <p>Step one is to submit your design requirements through our contact form or email. The more complete your initial information, the more accurate our initial quote will be. Essential information includes: style specifications (high-waist, flare, capri, etc.), fabric preferences or performance requirements, target quantity per style and color, size chart or target market sizing, desired delivery timeline, and any specific branding requirements (labels, hang tags, packaging). If you have technical drawings, photos of reference samples, or existing products you want to replicate, include these for clarity.</p>
        
        <p>Step two involves our review and quotation process. Within 24-48 hours of receiving your requirements, we provide a detailed quotation including fabric costs, production costs, sampling costs, and estimated shipping costs. The quotation specifies lead times for sampling and production, minimum order quantities, and payment terms. If any aspect of your requirements is unclear or requires clarification, we will ask questions before quoting to ensure accuracy. You may request revisions to the quotation if you want to adjust specifications to meet budget targets.</p>
        
        <p>Step three is sample development and approval. After quotation acceptance, we proceed with sample development, typically taking 15-20 days. Samples are shipped to you for review, and we provide measurement reports comparing samples to your specifications. You may approve samples as-is, request modifications, or proceed with additional sample rounds. Each sample round adds 7-10 days but ensures the final product meets your expectations. We recommend thorough testing of samples including fit models, wash testing, and wear testing before approval.</p>
        
        <p>Step four is production confirmation. Once samples are approved, we require a deposit to confirm production and initiate fabric procurement. Standard terms are 30% deposit with order confirmation and 70% before shipment. Production begins after deposit receipt and fabric availability is confirmed. We provide a production schedule with key milestones including cutting completion, sewing completion, and expected shipment date. Throughout production, we provide status updates and photos of goods in process.</p>
        
        <p>Step five is final inspection and shipment. Before shipment, we conduct final quality inspection using AQL standards and provide an inspection report for your review. Once inspection is approved, we finalize packaging and prepare shipping documentation. Balance payment is required before release of shipping documents. We provide all necessary documentation including commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading, certificates of origin, and any required certificates. Goods are released to your nominated freight forwarder or ours depending on agreed Incoterms.</p>
        
        <p>Throughout the process, our team is available to answer questions, provide guidance, and address any issues that arise. We understand that sourcing from a new manufacturer involves learning curves and are committed to making the process as smooth as possible. Clear communication and realistic expectations are key to successful production, and we work to establish both from the outset of our relationship.</p>
      </div>
